Introduction
------------

MimePrefs is a system-wide preference utility which allows
you to define how certain data types are handled when received
via the net (Downloaded, DCCed, attached to E-Mail).

The MimePrefs settings are currently honored by the following 
applications:

 - Voyager 3.x (http://v3.vapor.com/)
 - AmIRC 2.x and 3.x (http://www.vapor.com/amirc/)
 - MicroDot-II (http://www.vapor.com/md2/)

MimePrefs has an extensive online help facility using
MUI's bubble help. If you want information about a certain
entry field, just let the mouse pointer stay idle over it
and a description will pop up.


Revision history
----------------

0.3 beta
--------
- fixed view section enabling
- fixed a few typos in the help strings
- extended "Internal viewer" explanation
- added all variants of load/save functionality
- added default prefs
- added localisation support

0.4 beta
--------
- changed default prefs to contain a per-class
  definition and "Use class dir?" for the subtypes
- will now automatically whine when you select
  "Use class dir?" and there is no class wide
  specification, offering auto-creation of such
  an entry
- added Test functionality
- the PUBSCREEN/K args and tooltype now work

0.5 beta
--------
- fixed %p in test mode
- fixed a few more enable/disable problems
- "Use class Dir?" is now rejected if there is
  no class entry and the user rejects to
  create one
- added "Test view" mode which asks for a filename
  and does a test "view" with the currently selected
  MIME entry

0.6 beta
--------
- '%p' was broken in test view mode

0.7 beta
--------
- "Extensions:" is now disabled when a class
  specification is edited
- auto-created class entries no longer copy the
  file extensions from the currently selected
  entry
- improved bubble help texts
- will now use NList.mcc if installed
- fixed usedclasses definition

0.8 beta
--------
- added UseOldStyleLists keyword/tooltype
  to disable usage of Nlist.mcc
- the test window is now a workbench appwindow
  accepting dragged icons for the filename
- fixed PUBSCREEN and CREATEICONS shell args

1.0
---
- added support for vapor_update.library

1.1
---
- fixed Add button not working with newer MUI betas

1.2
---
[internal]

